THOUGHT: The new errors come from dereferencing `part.indices` without a null check in `Model.convertMesh`. Since `indices` is now nullable, I should guard those uses. A simple fix is to treat null as zero-length: skip its contribution to `numIndices`, and when filling mesh parts, only use `part.indices.length` and `put(part.indices)` if `indices` is non-null; otherwise, fall back to using `numVertices` and not writing indices. I’ll update Model.java accordingly and rerun the build to ensure the total NullAway error count drops from 454 to 453.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '262,285s/numIndices += part.indices.length;/if (part.indices != null) numIndices += part.indices.length;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/Model.java && sed -i '281,285c\      meshPart.offset = offset;
      meshPart.size = hasIndices && part.indices != null ? part.indices.length : numVertices;
      meshPart.mesh = mesh;
      if (hasIndices && part.indices != null) {
        mesh.getIndicesBuffer().put(part.indices);
      }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/g3d/Model.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output_2.log 2>&1 || echo "Gradle failed"; grep -E "ModelMeshPart.java:23|Model.java:26[24-9]|\serrors$" new_build_output_2.log | tail -n 20
```

